<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Apostol (1564)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1564</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Apostol of 1564 is the first precisely dated book printed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, produced by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-fyodorov">Ivan Fyodorov</a> and Pyotr Mstislavets at the Moscow Print Yard and completed on 1 March 1564. A liturgical book containing the Acts and Epistles of the apostles in Church Slavonic, it was printed with the support of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iv-of-russia">Ivan IV</a> and Metropolitan Macarius and marks the beginning of Russian book <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a>.</p></div>
